WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.395
Teacher midterm practice for C plus plus, question 7.

2
00:00:05.015 --> 00:00:07.977
What two lines does the first pair of nested loops print?

3
00:00:09.677 --> 00:00:12.136
The outer loop picks the row, i.

4
00:00:12.136 --> 00:00:15.223
The inner loop runs through the columns, j.

5
00:00:15.223 --> 00:00:20.827
Row one: j equals one gives one times one, plus one, minus six: minus four.

6
00:00:20.827 --> 00:00:24.258
j equals two gives two plus four minus six: zero.

7
00:00:24.878 --> 00:00:27.892
Then endl closes the row: minus four, zero.

8
00:00:28.512 --> 00:00:33.149
Row two: j equals one gives two plus one minus six: minus three.

9
00:00:33.149 --> 00:00:39.194
j equals two gives four plus four minus six: two. And endl: minus three, two.

10
00:00:40.794 --> 00:00:44.092
In nested loops, the outer loop variable stays fixed

11
00:00:44.092 --> 00:00:47.390
while the inner loop runs through all its values.

12
00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:49.922
So each printed row has one fixed i.

13
00:00:49.922 --> 00:00:54.162
Here the formula is j times i, plus j squared, minus six.

14
00:00:55.762 --> 00:00:58.392
So the output is minus four, zero on the first

15
00:00:58.392 --> 00:01:01.337
line, and minus three, two on the second.

16
00:01:02.157 --> 00:01:07.429
Swapping rows and columns. Each printed line has a fixed i, not a fixed j.

17
00:01:08.149 --> 00:01:12.640
Exam tip: draw a small grid with i down the side and j across the top,

18
00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.785
fill each cell from the formula, then read it off row by row.
